# Automated pull-request review — DISABLED STUB.
#
# pending: choose reviewer bot
#
# The preferred route is GitHub Copilot code review, which is a repository/organization setting and
# needs no workflow at all; see .github/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md section 3. This file exists for the
# other case: a self-hosted reviewer action, pinned to an exact model, whose output lives in this
# repository's own audit trail.
#
# Stored with a `.disabled` suffix on purpose. GitHub Actions only reads `*.yml` and `*.yaml` from
# .github/workflows/, so this cannot run, cannot fail, and cannot add a phantom status check while
# the choice of reviewer is still open. To enable:
#
#   1. pick the reviewer action and replace the `uses:` line below with an exact commit SHA
#      (a tag is mutable; a review bot with pull-request write access is not the place to trust a
#      moving reference);
#   2. add the API key as a repository secret and reference it under `env`;
#   3. `git mv .github/workflows/ai-review.yml.disabled .github/workflows/ai-review.yml`;
#   4. leave it out of the required status checks. An automated reviewer advises; it does not gate.
#      See .github/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md section 3.
#
# What a reviewer bot should be told to look for here, beyond ordinary code review:
#   * a theorem statement that drifted from what the pull-request description claims;
#   * a hypothesis added to an endpoint (a strengthened premise is how a bound quietly weakens);
#   * a new `#assert_axioms`-covered declaration that no census closure imports;
#   * numerical constants changed without the certificate that justifies them.

name: AI review

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]

permissions:
  contents: read
  pull-requests: write

jobs:
  review:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 20
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0
      # pending: choose reviewer bot — replace with the chosen action at a pinned commit SHA.
      - name: Automated review pass
        run: |
          echo 'No reviewer action configured yet; see .github/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md section 3.'
